'''''Armeria berlengensis''''' is a [[flowering plant]] in the family Plumbaginaceae. It is endemic to the [[Berlengas]], a [[Portugal|Portuguese]] [[archipelago]], where it occurs on the rocky [[granite|granitic]] slopes of the islands.<ref name="flora-on">{{cite web |title=Armeria berlengensis Daveau |url=https://flora-on.pt/#/1armeria+berlengensis |publisher=[[Flora-On]] |access-date=6 April 2021}}</ref> It is common on both [[Berlenga Grande Island]] and Farilhões Islets.

It is a shrub about {{cvt|40|cm}} in diameter, which flowers in April and May. The flowers are small, pale pink, and grouped into [[inflorescence]]s at the end of  long [[Pedicel (botany)|pedicels]].

